#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:0
msgid ""
"Create, inspect, verify, export, import, restore, and delete snap data "
"snapshots, with automatic retention and file exclusions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:8
msgid "Create data snapshots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:10
msgid ""
"A *snapshot* is a copy of the user, system and configuration data stored by "
"*snapd* for one or more snaps on your system. This data can be found in "
"`$HOME/snap/<snap-name>` and `/var/snap/<snap-name>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:12
msgid ""
"Snapshots are generated **manually** with the `snap save` command and "
"**automatically when a snap is removed** (unless `--purge` is used with "
"remove, in which case no snapshot is created). A snapshot can be used to "
"backup the state of your snaps, revert snaps to a previous state and to "
"restore a fresh snapd installation to a previously saved state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:14
msgid "Generating a snapshot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:16
msgid ""
"The `snap save` command creates a snapshot for all installed snaps, or if "
"declared individually, specific snaps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:18
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap save\n"
"Set  Snap         Age    Version               Rev   Size   Notes\n"
"30   core         1.00s  16-2.37~pre1          6229   250B  -\n"
"30   core18       886ms  18                    543    123B  -\n"
"30   go           483ms  1.10.7                3092   387B  -\n"
"30   vlc          529ms  3.0.6                 770   882kB  -\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:28
msgid ""
"Before using this command, stop any services for the snaps included in the "
"snapshot (`snap stop <snap-name>`) and close any running applications "
"provided by those snaps. Start them again once the snapshot has been saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:31
msgid ""
"Each snapshot has a unique ID, or revision, shown in the *Set* column above. "
"This value is unique to each *save* operation, regardless of the number of "
"snaps it includes. *Age* is the period of time since the snapshot was "
"created, while *Version* and *Rev* refer to the specific snap at the time of "
"the snapshot. *Size* is the amount of storage used by a snapshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:33
msgid ""
"If you'd rather not wait for the *save* operation to complete before "
"regaining access to your terminal, add the `--no-wait` argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:35
msgid ""
"You can see the state of your system's snapshots with the `snap saved` "
"command. Adding `--id=<set/unique ID>` allows you to query a specific "
"snapshot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:37
msgid ""
"$ snap saved --id=29\n"
"Set  Snap             Age    Version               Rev   Size   Notes\n"
"29   vlc              2h41m  3.0.6                 770   882kB  -\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:43
msgid ""
"Both the _saved_ and _check-snapshot_ commands accept a `–users=` option "
"with a comma-separated list of users to filter on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:46
msgid "What a snapshot stores"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:48
msgid ""
"A snapshot is a copy of the user, system and configuration data stored by "
"*snapd* for one or more snaps on your system. For each snap, this data can "
"be found in `$HOME/snap/<snap-name>` and `/var/snap/<snap-name>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:50
msgid ""
"More specifically, these are locations that snapped application access "
"through the following environment variables from within the snap:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:52
msgid "System-wide locations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:53
msgid "**SNAP_COMMON** ( `/var/snap/<snap-name>/common `)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:54
msgid "**SNAP_DATA** (`/var/snap/<snap-name>/<revision>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:56
msgid "User-specific locations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:57
msgid "**SNAP_USER_COMMON** (`/home/<username>/snap/<snap-name>/common`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:58
msgid "**SNAP_USER_DATA** (`/home/<username>/snap/<snap-name>/<revision>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:60
msgid ""
"[snapd _2.77_+] Data residing in mount points under the snap data "
"directories listed above is excluded from all snapshots, whether created "
"manually with `snap save` or automatically when a snap is removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:62
msgid ""
"It's important to note that **SNAP_DATA** and **SNAP_USER_DATA** place their "
"data within a directory specific to each snap {ref}`revision <explanation-"
"how-snaps-work-revisions>`, whereas  **SNAP_COMMON** and  "
"**SNAP_USER_COMMON** do not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:64
msgid ""
"You need to be aware of what data is copied forward when you move from one "
"revision to the next and which data will be restored if you switch to a "
"previous snapshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:66
msgid ""
"When you move from one revision to the next, the revision-specific contents "
"of  **SNAP_DATA** and  **SNAP_USER_DATA** are copied into new directories "
"for the new revision. The contents of  **SNAP_COMMON** and  "
"**SNAP_USER_COMMON** remain the same. A snapshot **only** includes the data "
"for the installed revision, plus the contents of the two **COMMON** "
"directories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:68
msgid "When a snapshot is restored:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:69
msgid ""
"The contents of   **SNAP_COMMON** and  **SNAP_USER_COMMON** will be "
"_overwritten_ and restored to their state when the restored snapshot was "
"created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:71
msgid ""
"The revision-specific contents of **SNAP_DATA** and  **SNAP_USER_DATA** will "
"be copied into and _overwrite_ the contents of the revision-specific "
"directory of the currently installed revision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:73
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Data locations <interfaces-data-locations>` for more details on "
"how these locations are intended to be used by a snap, and see {ref}`Inside "
"a snapshot <ref-create-data-snapshots_inside-a-snapshot>` to see how they're "
"stored within a snapshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:75
msgid "Excluding data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:77
msgid "Static exclusion via meta/snapshots.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:78
msgid ""
"A snap can use the [`meta/snapshots.yaml`](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/"
"snapcraft/latest/reference/snapshots/) file to exclude data from snapshots. "
"This config file contains a single `exclude` keyword which lists one or more "
"wildcard patterns of files or directories to exclude from snapshots. The "
"wildcard patterns must start with the **SNAP_DATA**, **SNAP_COMMON**, "
"**SNAP_USER_DATA**, or **SNAP_USER_COMMON** variable and cannot include `[`, "
"`]`, `{`, `}`, `?`, or `**`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:80
msgid ""
"Since the exclusions are defined in the snap package, they do not change "
"between snapshots and are fixed for a given revision. These static "
"exclusions apply to both manual and automatic snapshots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:82
msgid ""
"# meta/snapshots.yaml\n"
"exclude:\n"
"  - $SNAP_DATA/*.png\n"
"  - $SNAP_COMMON/stories\n"
"  - $SNAP_USER_DATA/data/transactions.db\n"
"  - $SNAP_USER_COMMON/*/*\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:91
msgid "Dynamic exclusion via snapd REST API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:92
msgid ""
"A snapshot can also be created using a POST request to the [`/v2/snaps`]"
"(https://snapcraft.io/docs/reference/development/snapd-rest-api/#/"
"Asynchronous/manageSnaps) REST API endpoint. The request body includes a "
"`snapshot-options` field that can be used to list snap-specific paths of "
"files or directories to exclude from the snapshot. These paths follow the "
"same patterns as mentioned above for the `meta/snapshots.yaml` file. The "
"exclusion path patterns are specified per request and can vary across "
"snapshots. This dynamic path exclusion is only available for manual "
"snapshots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:94
msgid ""
"{\n"
"    \"action\": \"snapshot\",\n"
"    \"snaps\": [\"<snap1>\", \"<snap2>\"],\n"
"    \"snapshot-options\": {\n"
"        \"<snap1>\": {\"exclude\": [\"<pattern1>\", \"<pattern2>\"]},\n"
"        \"<snap2>\": {\"exclude\": [\"<pattern3>\"]}\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:105
msgid "Verifying a snapshot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:107
msgid ""
"To verify the integrity of a snapshot, use the `check-snapshot` command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:109
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap check-snapshot 30\n"
"Snapshot #30 verified successfully.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:114
msgid "Exporting and importing a snapshot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:116
msgid ""
"By default, snapshots are maintained and stored on the system that created "
"them. However, to help with backup and recovery, individual snapshots can "
"also be exported and restored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:118
msgid ""
"To export a snapshot, use the `snap export-snapshot <set-id> <new-filename>` "
"command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:120
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap export-snapshot 30 my-snapshot.zip\n"
"Exported snapshot #30 into \"my-snapshot.zip\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:125
msgid ""
"The resultant snapshot file is a _zip_ archive that contains two _json_ "
"files to validate the snapshot and a _zip_ archive containing the user, "
"system and configuration data for the specific revision of the snap "
"installed when the snapshot was created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:127
msgid ""
"To import a previously exported snap shot, use the `snap import-snapshot` "
"command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:129
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap import-snapshot mysnapshot\n"
"Imported snapshot as #30\n"
"Set  Snap  Age    Version  Rev   Size    Notes\n"
"30   vlc   3d02h  1.11.13  4286  255B  -\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:136
msgid ""
"If the snapshot with the same snapshot identifier exists, the import will "
"overwrite it. If the snapshot doesn't exist, it will be imported and "
"assigned a new snapshot identifier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:138
msgid "Restoring a snapshot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:140
msgid ""
"The `restore` command replaces the current user, system and configuration "
"data with the corresponding data from the specified snapshot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:142
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap restore 30\n"
"Restored snapshot #30.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:148
msgid ""
"Before using this command, make sure the snap is installed, then stop its "
"services (`snap stop <snap-name>`) and close any running applications "
"provided by that snap. Start them again once the snapshot has been "
"successfully restored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:151
msgid ""
"By default, this command restores all the data for all the snaps in a "
"snapshot. You can restore data for specific snaps by simply listing them "
"after the command and for specific users with the `--users=<usernames>` "
"argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:153
msgid ""
"[snapd _2.77_+] Existing {ref}`mount-control <interfaces-mount-control-"
"interface>` mount points under snap data directories are preserved when a "
"snapshot is restored and are not overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:155
msgid ""
"Excluding a snap's system and configuration data from *snap restore* is not "
"currently possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:157
msgid "Deleting a snapshot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:159
msgid ""
"The `forget` command deletes a snapshot. This operation removes a snapshot "
"from local storage and can not be undone:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:161
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap forget 30\n"
"Snapshot #30 forgotten.\n"
"$ snap saved --id=30\n"
"No snapshots found.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:168
msgid ""
"By default, this command deletes all the data for all the snaps in a "
"snapshot. You can delete the data for specific snaps by listing them after "
"the command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:171
msgid "Automatic snapshots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:173
msgid ""
"Apart from on [Ubuntu Core](https://www.ubuntu.com/core) devices, where the "
"feature is disabled by default, a snapshot is generated automatically when a "
"snap is removed. These snapshots are retained for 31 days before being "
"deleted automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:175
msgid ""
"To see which snapshots are generated automatically,  look for `auto` in the "
"*Notes* column output from *snap saved*:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:177
msgid ""
"$ snap saved\n"
"Set  Snap              Age    Version               Rev   Size   Notes\n"
"30   go                25d5h  1.10.7                3092   387B  -\n"
"30   vlc               25d0h  3.0.6                 770   882kB  -\n"
"31   vlc               529ms  3.0.6                 770   882kB  auto\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:185
msgid ""
"As with manual snapshots, automatically generated snapshots can be manually "
"deleted with `snap forget <set-id>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:187
msgid ""
"Automatic snapshot retention time is configured with the "
"`snapshots.automatic.retention` {ref}`system option <how-to-guides-manage-"
"snaps-set-system-options>`. The value needs to be greater than 24 hours:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:189
msgid "snap set system snapshots.automatic.retention=30h\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:193
msgid "To disable automatic snapshots, set the retention time to `no`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:195
msgid "snap set system snapshots.automatic.retention=no\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:199
msgid ""
"Disabling automatic snapshots will *not* affect pre-existing automatically "
"generated snapshots, only those generated by the removal of subsequent snaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:201
msgid "Automatic snapshots require snap version _2.39+_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:204
msgid "Inside a snapshot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:206
msgid ""
"On Ubuntu-based systems, snapshots are stored in the `/var/lib/snapd/"
"snapshots` directory and are both stored and exported as a *zip* file. This "
"zip file contains the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:208
msgid ""
"<snap-snapshot-zip>\n"
"├── <snapshot-number>_<snap-name>_<revision>.zip\n"
"└────── archive.tgz\n"
"    │   ├── <revision-number>\n"
"    │       └── $SNAP_DATA (/var/snap/<snap-name>-<revision>)\n"
"    │   └── common\n"
"    │       └── $SNAP_COMMON (/var/snap/<snap-name>/common)\n"
"    ├── meta.json\n"
"    ├── meta.sha3_384\n"
"    └── user\n"
"        └── <username>.tgz\n"
"            ├── <revision-number>\n"
"            │   └── $SNAP_USER_DATA (/home/<username>/snap/<snap-name>/"
"<revision>)\n"
"            └── common\n"
"                └── $SNAP_USER_COMMON(/home/<username>/<snap-name>)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/create-data-snapshots.md:227
msgid ""
"**meta.json**: describes the contents of the snapshot, alongside its "
"configuration and checksums for the archives."
msgstr ""
